</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Demographics and Additional Information</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For users) Would you personally use AI-powered chatbots to answer your mental health-related questions?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For users) From whom do you prefer to seek help, a human therapist or an AI-powered chatbot, when you have mental health-related questions?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For therapists) As a mental health professional, would you recommend AI-powered chatbots to patients for obtaining general mental health information?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For therapists) As a mental health professional, would you recommend AI-powered chatbots to patients for obtaining answers and advice similar to what is provided in a psychotherapy session?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Do you have any opinion on using chatbots for mental health related purposes that you would like to share with us?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For users) Have you ever received services from a mental health professional, such as a psychologist, counselor, therapist, or psychiatrist? If so, for how long?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(7)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(For therapists) How long have you been a therapist for?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(8)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What is your age?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(9)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What gender do you identify with?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(10)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which group(s) do you identify with (select all that apply)?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(11)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Do you live in the U.S.?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(12)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Which state do you live in?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(13)</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">What is your highest level of education attained?</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>CLMM Specification</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model the ordinal response <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{ij}\in\{-4,-3,\dots,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{ij}\in\{-4,-3,\dots,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the
rating difference between large language model (LLM) outputs and human responses,
using a cumulative link mixed model (CLMM) with a logit link.
Let <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> index participants and <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> index treatments (<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">gpt</span>, <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">gemini</span>, <span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">llama</span>).
The cumulative probability that participant <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> under treatment <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> rates at or below category <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr(D_{ij}\leq k\mid\mathbf{x}_{ij},u_{i})=\text{logit}^{-1}\!\left(\theta_{k}-\eta_{ij}-u_{i}\right),\quad k=-4,\dots,3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext>logit</mtext><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(D_{ij}\leq k\mid\mathbf{x}_{ij},u_{i})=\text{logit}^{-1}\!\left(\theta_{k}-\eta_{ij}-u_{i}\right),\quad k=-4,\dots,3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are threshold (cutpoint) parameters, and
<math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is a participant-specific random intercept.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The linear predictor <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is specified as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta_{ij}=\alpha_{\text{gemini}}I(\text{Treatment}=\text{gemini})+\alpha_{\text{llama}}I(\text{Treatment}=\text{llama})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>gemini</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Treatment</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>gemini</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>llama</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Treatment</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>llama</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta_{ij}=\alpha_{\text{gemini}}I(\text{Treatment}=\text{gemini})+\alpha_{\text{llama}}I(\text{Treatment}=\text{llama})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{m}\beta_{m}X_{ijm}+\sum_{\ell}\gamma_{\ell}\big(\text{Treatment}\times\text{Experience}\big)_{ij\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mtext>Treatment</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext>Experience</mtext><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{m}\beta_{m}X_{ijm}+\sum_{\ell}\gamma_{\ell}\big(\text{Treatment}\times\text{Experience}\big)_{ij\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Experience</span> refers to therapy experience,
<math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{ijm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{ijm}</annotation></semantics></math> are demographic covariates (education, age, race, state, gender, and
the indicator <span id="A3.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">can_distinguish</span>), and
the interaction terms capture moderation by therapy experience.</p>
</div>
</section>
